section("AO","RESUME EVIDENCE","[RESUME_EVIDENCE.md](RESUME_EVIDENCE.md) provides six candidate bullets traceable to dataset, GPU, camera, formal/broker and real Bedrock artifacts. Strongest claims concern measured scale and execution. Avoid claiming GNN superiority, significant RL improvement, whole-system GPU speedup, real camera/disaster validity, broad synthesis generalization or native Alexa deployment.")
section("AP","KNOWN LIMITATIONS","Synthetic disaster equations; one training topology; limited program/hazard families; sparse positive camera classes and a failed congestion head; imperfect anomaly/OOD detection; empirical adaptive selection mismatch; offline RL with deployment cadence mismatch; manually encoded SMT guards; bounded graph-hop placement; local single-player owner model; component GPU acceleration; deterministic fixture submission; template versus language synthesis distinction; no measured multi-model dollar-cost routing.")
section("AQ","UNVERIFIED PATHS","Native Alexa+ preview/client deployment; physical speech hardware/service reliability; authenticated real Google reads/writes; TensorRT/custom kernels; engineering-grade hazard safety; real camera data; Northbank learned-model transfer to external geography/data; independently learned responder agents; learned meta-policy; multi-model routing; two/three-attempt paid repair; movable generators/shelter supply optimization. These limitations remain explicit and do not invalidate the executed paths.")
